^SAMPLE = GSM2827720
!Sample_title = Empty control Rep 1
!Sample_geo_accession = GSM2827720
!Sample_status = Public on Dec 01 2018
!Sample_submission_date = Oct 23 2017
!Sample_last_update_date = May 15 2019
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = STAT1-/- fibroblasts
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = tissue: Skin
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = genotype: STAT1-/-
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = expression: empty control vector
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = Naïve STAT1-/- fibroblasts were spinoculated with lentivirus containing CMV-driven IFI6 or empty control vector. The plasmid backbone also contains TagRFP and a puromycin-resistance cassette. Two days after spinoculation, cells were split into media containing 4 ug/mL puromycin. Cells were passaged at a 1:4 split for the indicated number of passages, No additional manipulations occurred prior to processing cells for RNA extraction.
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = STAT1-/- fibroblasts were grown in RPMI supplemented with 10% FBS, 1X non-essential amino acids, and 4 ug/mL puromycin.
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = RNA was harvested using RNeasy Mini Kit (Qiagen #74106) following the manufacturer's instructions. Integrity was verified using the Agilent 2100 Bioanalyzer. All samples had a RIN score of 8 or higher.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Four micrograms of total DNAse-treated RNA were then prepared with the TruSeq Stranded Total RNA LT Sample Prep Kit from Illumina (Illumina  #RS-122). Poly-A RNA was purified and fragmented before strand specific cDNA synthesis.  cDNA were then A-tailed and indexed adapters were ligated. After adapter ligation, samples were PCR amplified and purified with AmpureXP beads, then validated again on the Agilent 2100 Bioanalyzer. Before being normalized and pooled, samples were quantified by Qubit then run on the Illumina Hiseq 2500 using SBS v3 reagents.
!Sample_description = Cells stably expressing empty control vector for 7 passages
!Sample_data_processing = Single-end 50 bp read length Fastq files were checked for quality using fastqc and fastq_screen
!Sample_data_processing = Reads were quality trimmed using fastq-mcf (ea-utils).
!Sample_data_processing = Trimmed fastq files were mapped to human genome using TopHat
!Sample_data_processing = Duplicates were marked using picard-tools
!Sample_data_processing = Read counts were generated using featureCounts (subread) for coding genes from gencode (v19)
!Sample_data_processing = Normalized read counts generated using edgeR
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: hg19
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: tab delimited txt files that includes normalized read counts for each sample per gene
!Sample_platform_id = GPL16791
!Sample_contact_name = John,,Schoggins
!Sample_contact_email = John.Schoggins@UTSouthwestern.edu
!Sample_contact_laboratory = Schoggins Lab
!Sample_contact_department = Department of Microbiology
!Sample_contact_institute = UT Southwester Medical Center
!Sample_contact_address = 5323 Harry Hines Blvd
!Sample_contact_city = Dallas
!Sample_contact_state = Texas
!Sample_contact_zip/postal_code = 75390-9032
!Sample_contact_country = USA
!Sample_instrument_model = Illumina HiSeq 2500
!Sample_library_selection = cDNA
!Sample_library_source = transcriptomic
!Sample_library_strategy = RNA-Seq
